IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wills-making`

-- Wills Act 1970 (WA), ss 6, 7, 8, 10, 11, 13 (deleted), 14, 14A, 15, 16, 20, 26, 27, 32, 33, 40 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_wills-act-1970_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts used are from the workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-{chloe,jake,daniel}/facts.json. The lives do not
-- date Graham's, Giuseppe's or Maria's wills; those cases take 1 June 2040 as a HYPOTHETICAL date.

§ `fixtures`

`signed by me before two witnesses together` MEANS `My will's signing` WITH
    `it is in writing` IS TRUE
    `I signed it` IS TRUE
    `someone signed it for me, in my presence and at my direction` IS FALSE
    `the signature shows I meant it to give effect to the will` IS TRUE
    `witnesses present together when I signed or acknowledged` IS 2
    `of them, unable to see and attest that I signed` IS 0
    `the witnesses signed in my presence` IS TRUE
    `a witness, or a witness's spouse, takes a gift under it` IS FALSE

